menu "EmuCON command line"

config CONF_WITH_CLI
	bool "Include the built-in EmuCON command interpreter"
	default n if TARGET_192
	default y
	help
	  EmuCON is a small command line interpreter built into the image.
	  It is reachable from the desktop, and is started directly when the
	  AES is not included.

config CONF_EXTERNAL_CLI
	bool "Load EmuCON from the boot drive instead of linking it in"
	depends on CONF_WITH_CLI && !ARCH_COLDFIRE
	depends on ((ARCH_ARM || ARCH_X86_64 || BUILD_TOOLCHAIN_ELF) && CONF_WITH_ELF_LOADER) || (ARCH_M68K && !BUILD_TOOLCHAIN_ELF && CONF_WITH_PRG_LOADER)
	default y if TARGET_RPI_KERNEL || TARGET_VIRT_ARM_KERNEL || TARGET_VIRT_M68K_KERNEL || TARGET_PC_X86_64_EFI
	help
	  Build EmuCON as an ordinary program, emucon.tos, and leave it out
	  of the kernel image.  The kernel starts it with Pexec() from the
	  root directory of the boot drive (EMUCON.TOS) when it has no AES to
	  start: as the console of the image, and as the early console.

	  The program is the standalone EmuCON of cli/Makefile, built with the
	  translations of all the languages of po/LINGUAS; it uses the
	  language in the LANG variable that the kernel puts in its
	  environment.  It has to be on the boot drive: "make test-dir",
	  "make test-hd" and the Raspberry Pi archives put it there.

	  Needs the loader of the program's format: ELF on ARM, x86-64 and
	  with the bare m68k-elf toolchain (which makes ELF files, so it
	  needs CONF_WITH_ELF_LOADER), PRG with the other m68k toolchains.
	  Not offered for ColdFire, which the standalone build does not
	  support (its Line-A calls differ).

	  On by default for the images that are loaded into RAM from a disk
	  (Raspberry Pi, virt-arm, virt-m68k, x86-64).  On x86-64 the program
	  is the x32 EmuCON (see the top level Makefile), which runs as an
	  ordinary ring-3 process; without this option the image embeds it.

endmenu
